 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: Monostatos's \"Nun stolzer Jüngling\" (the libretto has \"Na\"), the spellings \"Sclave\", \"Füssen\", \"büssen\", \"wusst'\" and \"auszuspüren\" (the libretto has \"aufzuspüren\"), the print's apostrophes in \"glaub'\", \"schling'\", \"wär'\", \"verweg'nen\", \"Frev'ler\", \"Bedenk'\", \"wollt'\", \"verhofft'\" and \"Sohlenstreich'\", Pamina's and Tamino's lines as the print gives them (Pamina \"Er ist's! Ich glaub' es kaum. Er ist's!\", Tamino \"Sie ist's! Sie ist's! Es ist kein Traum!\"), and Monostatos's \"Ach, Herr! ach, Herr!\". The chorus (sopranos, altos, tenors, basses: \"Was soll das heissen?\", \"Es lebe Sarastro\" and the closing \"Wenn Tugend und Gerechtigkeit\") is heard with the piano and has no phrases here. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
